(B)(a) Reagents:
(i) aqueous $Br_2$ (oxidation of an aldose to an acid);
(ii) HBr with peroxide followed by hydrolysis (anti-Markovnikov) / $B_2H_6$ then $H_2O_2$/OH$^-$ (hydroboration--oxidation);
(iii) $H_2$, Ni/Pd/Pt / $LiAlH_4$ / $NaBH_4$ (reduction).
(b) Acid-catalysed hydration of an alkene proceeds in three steps:
1. Protonation of the alkene by $H_3O^+$ to form a carbocation;
2. Nucleophilic attack of water on the carbocation to give a protonated alcohol;
3. Deprotonation of the protonated alcohol by water to form the alcohol and regenerate $H_3O^+$.
